I'd been ruminating on the workstation version, but rather than 3-D,
I'd just like to see _much bigger_ levels.  On my Amiga, with
(relatively) low res and good color, I'd like to split the screen in
half with a one dot per location map of the known level on the left
half, giving a 320X by 200Y maze overall, and the local area where my
character is at present on the right, preferably with double sized
characters so that ...

>And someone has to do the dirty job -- draw all those monsters.

the monsters/features can be drawn bigger and with more detail.

Of course, on the Amiga and other machines with a fast bit-blitter
(fast window redraw), the stats lines, the overview, and the local
scene could each be a separate window (or, on the Amiga, screen), with
only one (fully) visible at a time.

My goal would be levels (probably with non-box shaped rooms) that each
took about an hour to explore fully, so I wouldn't have to read about
all these newbies pounding on the wizard before the game
implementation is even finished.  ;-)

Just daydreaming - the limits of my ambition while I grow my new arm
are hitting the space bar in rn.
